  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required to trace this contract mismatch:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n1. `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 core: `request_body_to_args()` (embed logic, `.get(field.alias)` extraction, None/missing-key \u2192 default-vs-required branching) and `solve_dependencies()` (wires parsed body into the dependency graph)\n2. `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 Content-Type negotiation: `is_body_form` branch choosing `await request.form()` vs `await request.json()`, and the `json.JSONDecodeError` handling\n3. `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v2 compat shim: `ModelField.validate()` wraps `TypeAdapter.validate_python()` (this is where v2's stricter/smart-union coercion differs from v1), plus `field_annotation_is_scalar`/`is_sequence_field` helpers that decide if something is treated as a body field at all\n4. `fastapi/params.py` \u2014 `Body`/`Form`/`File` field definitions (`embed`, `media_type` defaults) that drive the request_body_to_args branching\n5. `fastapi/exceptions.py` \u2014 `RequestValidationError`, the 422 payload shape\n6. `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, FastAPI's own canonical Python\u2192JSON-safe conversion (relevant as the \"recommended fix\" reference for client-side encoding)\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n1. `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_request()`/`encode_json()`: plain `json.dumps()` with **no default encoder**, `encode_urlencoded_data()` for form data\n2. `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__` calling `encode_request()`, header auto-population (`_prepare`)\n3. `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 `build_request()` path that assembles `content`/`data`/`json` into a `Request`\n4. `httpx/_types.py` \u2014 `RequestData`/`RequestContent`/`RequestFiles` type aliases defining what shapes httpx accepts\n\nThis gives the full picture needed to document drift points: httpx's `encode_json` is bare `json.dumps` (chokes on datetime/UUID/Enum from `model.dict()`/`model_dump()` without `mode=\"json\"`), while FastAPI's Pydantic v2 `TypeAdapter.validate_python` in `_compat.py` applies smart-union coercion and distinguishes \"missing key\" from \"explicit null\" per `request_body_to_args`'s required/default branching in `dependencies/utils.py`.",
